hadiths[44]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1791","Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas that he was behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from Jam, and he continued to say talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah."
"1792","It was recited to Sufyan: I heard Muhammad ibn Abi Harmalah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah."
"1793","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Ata informed me, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took al-Fadl ibn Abbas behind him from Jam. Ata said: Ibn Abbas informed me that al-Fadl informed him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, continued to say talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah."
"1794","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Abu az-Zubayr informed me, Abu Mabad informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas informing from al-Fadl, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the evening of Arafah and the morning of Jam to the people when we moved forth: Calmness upon you, while holding back his she-camel, until when he entered Mina, when he descended Muhassir, he said: Upon you is the pebbles of khadhf with which the Jamrah is stoned. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gestured with his hand as a person throws. Rawh and al-Bursani said: On the evening of Arafah and the morning of Jam, and both said: When they moved forth."
"1795","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood in the Kabah and glorified and magnified Allah and supplicated Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and sought forgiveness, and did not bow nor prostrate."
"1796","Hujayn and Yunus narrated to us, both saying: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Abu Mabad, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, who was the companion behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said on the evening of Arafah and the morning of Jam to the people when they moved forth: Calmness upon you, while holding back his she-camel, until when he entered Muhassir, and it is of Mina, he said: Upon you is the pebbles of khadhf with which the Jamrah is stoned. And he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, continued to say talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah."
"1797","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali informed me, from Abbas ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, visited Abbas in a desert land of ours, and we had a small dog and a she-ass grazing. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Asr while they were before him, and they were neither moved back nor driven away."
"1798","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Abu at-Tufayl, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas that he was behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from Jam to Mina, and he continued to say talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah."
"1799","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Mubarak informed us, Layth ibn Sad informed us, Abd Rabbihi ibn Said narrated to us, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Abdullah ibn Nafi ibn al-Amya, from Rabiah ibn al-Harith, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Prayer is two by two; you make tashahhud in every two rakahs, and implore, and humble yourself, and show need, then raise your hands, saying: You raise them to your Lord with their palms facing your face, saying: O Lord, O Lord. Whoever does not do that, he said regarding it a severe saying."
"1800","Yazid ibn Abi Hakim al-Adani narrated to us, al-Hakam meaning Ibn Aban narrated to me, he said: I heard Ikrimah saying: al-Fadl ibn Abbas said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, poured forth, and I was with him, and we reached the mountain pass, he descended and performed ablution, then we rode until we came to Muzdalifah."
"1801","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Abd Allah ibn Abi Najih narrated to me, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah or from Mujahid ibn Jabr, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas: My brother Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, who was with him when he entered it, narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray inside the Kabah, but when he entered it he fell prostrate between the two pillars, then sat supplicating."
"1802","Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: Al-Fadl ibn Abbas informed me that he was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he poured forth from Jam. He said: So he poured forth with tranquility upon him. He said: And he continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah. And on one occasion he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: Al-Fadl ibn Abbas informed us, he said: I witnessed both pourings-forth with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he poured forth with tranquility upon him while holding back his camel. He said: And he continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah, several times."
"1803","Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, who was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he poured forth from Arafah. He said: He saw the people rushing, so he ordered his crier who called out: Righteousness does not consist in rushing horses and camels, so calmness is incumbent upon you."
"1804","Yaqub narrated to us, Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle who said: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed me, he said: Aishah and Umm Salamah, the two wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake in the morning in a state of major impurity from his family, then wash before praying Fajr, then fast that day. He said: So I mentioned that to Abu Hurayrah, and he said: I do not know; Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, informed me of that."
"1805","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ibn Abbas, from his brother Al-Fadl who said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Jam to Mina, and while he was traveling a Bedouin having his beautiful daughter riding behind him came across him, and he was traveling alongside him. He said: So I kept looking at her, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at me and turned my face away from her face, then I looked again and he turned my face away from her face, until he did that three times while I would not stop. And he continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"1806","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Qays informed us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abbas, from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued uttering the Talbiyah on the Day of Sacrifice until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"1807","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl, that he was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah."
"1808","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas who said: I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he uttered the Talbiyah during Hajj until he stoned the Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice."
"1809","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amir al-Ahwal and Jabir al-Jufi and Ibn Ata, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice."
"1810","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jabir and Amir al-Ahwal and Ibn Ata, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that Al-Fadl ibn Abbas was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he continued uttering the Talbiyah on the Day of Sacrifice until he stoned the Jamrah."
"1811","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Mushash informed me, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the weak ones of Banu Hashim, he ordered them to hasten from Jam by night."
"1812","Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas or from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father was overtaken by Islam while he is a very old man who cannot remain firm upon his mount, so shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Tell me, if he owed a debt and you paid it on his behalf, would that suffice him? He said: Yes. He said: Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father."
"1813","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq who said: I heard Sulayman ibn Yasar, Al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man asked him and said: My father or my mother is a very old man who cannot perform Hajj, and he mentioned the hadith."
"1814","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me, from al-Ahwal and Jabir al-Jufi and Ibn Ata, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl, that he was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice."
"1815","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said, Abd Allah said, and I heard it myself from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad: Hafs narrated to us, from Jafar, from his father, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah, and he stoned it with seven pebbles, pronouncing Takbir with every pebble."
"1816","Yala and Muhammad, the two sons of Ubayd, narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafat with Usamah ibn Zayd riding behind him, and his she-camel moved about with him while he was standing at Arafat before pouring forth, while he was raising his hands not exceeding his head. Then when he poured forth he traveled gently until he reached Jam, then he poured forth from Jam with Al-Fadl riding behind him. Al-Fadl said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah."
"1817","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali narrated to me, from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Abbas while we were in a desert land of ours, and he stood to pray, he said, I think he said Asr, with a small dog of ours and a grazing donkey in front of him, with nothing between him and them blocking between him and them."
"1818","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas: Al-Fadl ibn Abbas narrated to me, he said: A woman from Khatham came and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father has been overtaken by the obligation of Allah Almighty in Hajj while he is a very old man who cannot remain firm upon his mount. He said: Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father."
"1819","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Ibn Abbas used to report that Al-Fadl ibn Abbas informed him that he entered the House with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray inside the House when he entered it, but when he came out and descended he bowed two rakahs by the door of the House."
"1820","Yahya ibn Zakariya, meaning Ibn Abi Zaidah, narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had Usamah ibn Zayd ride behind him from Arafah until he reached Jam, and had Al-Fadl ibn Abbas ride behind him from Jam until he reached Mina. Ibn Abbas said: And Al-Fadl ibn Abbas informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah."
"1821","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Ibn Bakr, they said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that Abu Mabad, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, informed him, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said on the evening of Arafah and the morning of Jam to the people when they set out: Calmness is incumbent upon you, while he was holding back his she-camel, until when he entered Mina, when he descended into Muhassir, he said: You must use the pebbles of Khadhf with which the Jamrah is stoned, with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gesturing with his hand as a person throws."
"1822","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab, Sulayman ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl, that a woman from Khatham said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), my father has been overtaken by the obligation of Allah in Hajj while he is a very old man who cannot sit upright upon the back of his camel. He said: Then perform Hajj on his behalf."
"1823","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Ahmad, meaning al-Zubayri, with the meaning, narrated to us, they said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas. Abu Ahmad said: Al-Fadl ibn Abbas narrated to me, he said: I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he poured forth from Muzdalifah, with a Bedouin traveling alongside him and his handsome daughter riding behind him. Al-Fadl said: So I began looking at her, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my face turning me away from her. And he continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"1824","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ulathah narrated to us, from Maslamah al-Juhani, he said: I heard him narrating from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and a gazelle appeared and turned to its side, so I embraced it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, did you take it as an evil omen? He said: An omen is only what moves you forward or holds you back."
"1825","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"1826","Ismail narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us, from Raja ibn Haywah who said: Yala ibn Uqbah built in Ramadan, then woke in the morning in a state of major impurity, so he met Abu Hurayrah and asked him. He said: Break your fast. He said: Shall I not fast this day and make it up with another day? He said: Break your fast. So he went to Marwan and told him, and Marwan sent Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith to the Mother of the Believers and asked her. She said: He would wake in the morning among us in a state of major impurity without a wet dream, then wake fasting. So he returned to Marwan and told him. He said: Confront Abu Hurayrah with her. He said: Neighbor, neighbor. He said: I adjure you to confront him with it. He said: So he met him and told him. He said: I did not hear it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Al-Fadl ibn Abbas only informed me of it. He said: Then afterwards I met Raja and said: Who narrated the hadith of Yala to you? He said: He narrated it to me himself."
"1827","Muhammad, who is Ibn Jafar, and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf, from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl, that he was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Sacrifice, and he continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah. Rawh said: During Hajj. Rawh said, meaning in his hadith, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Yusuf ibn Mahak, both of them said: Ibn Mahak."
"1828","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Kathir ibn Shinzhir narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that he was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Sacrifice, and there was a slave girl behind her father. So I began looking at her, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began turning my face away from her. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued from Jam to Mina uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice."
"1829","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, Azrah narrated to me, from al-Shabi, that Al-Fadl narrated to him that he was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Arafah, and his mount did not lift its foot proceeding until he reached Jam. He said: And al-Shabi narrated to me that Usamah narrated to him that he was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Jam, and his mount did not lift its foot proceeding until he stoned the Jamrah."
"1830","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood inside the Kabah and glorified Allah, pronounced Takbir, supplicated Allah and sought His forgiveness, and did not bow nor prostrate."
"1831","Marwan ibn Shuja narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had Usamah ride behind him from Arafat to Jam, and had Al-Fadl ride behind him from Jam to Mina, and he informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"1832","Kathir ibn Hisham informed us, he said: Furat narrated to us, Abd al-Karim narrated to us, from Sad ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he continued uttering the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"1833","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Israil narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas or from Al-Fadl ibn Abbas or one of them from his companion, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends to perform Hajj, let him hasten, for a stray animal may stray, a sick person may fall ill, and a need may arise."
"1834","Waki narrated to us, Abu Israil al-Absi narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Al-Fadl or one of them from the other, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends Hajj, let him hasten, for a sick person may fall ill, a stray animal may stray, and a need may present itself."
